issue.body:
Related: #180250

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: the release candidate quota check can remain running beyond `--max-wait-seconds` when GitHub stops sending response headers or the JSON body; an unfinished error response can also keep the process alive after it reports HTTP 403.

## User Impact

User impact: release operators get a bounded failure and a closed connection instead of a stuck quota-check step. There is no end-user behavior change. Quota thresholds, reset handling, request headers, and HTTP error diagnostics remain unchanged.

## Why This Change Was Made

The existing deadline guarded the next reset sleep but did not cancel network I/O. Each request now shares one abort signal across fetching headers and consuming JSON, using the remaining existing wait budget. Cleanup clears the timer and releases any unread error response. The timer delay is capped at Node's supported maximum so a very large configured budget cannot overflow into an immediate timeout; the existing five-hour default is unaffected.

## Evidence

Executed the actual helper CLI with Node 24.22.2 against an isolated loopback HTTP server, using only a synthetic token. Both revisions made real HTTP requests; no fetch, clock, or response parser was mocked in this proof. The container had no external network, ran as nonroot, and was limited to 512 MiB and half a CPU.

```bash
GH_TOKEN=fixture-token GITHUB_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:<port> \
  node scripts/wait-for-github-api-quota.mjs --max-wait-seconds 1
```

| Server behavior | Base `e792f74abfeaa` | Fixed |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Accepts request; never sends headers | Still running with connection open at 2.517 s; proof cleanup kills it | Natural exit 1 in 1.121 s; connection closed |
| Sends 200 and partial JSON; never finishes body | Still running with connection open at 2.509 s; proof cleanup kills it | Natural exit 1 in 1.078 s; connection closed |
| Sends 403 and partial JSON; never finishes body | Prints HTTP 403, then remains running with connection open at 2.559 s | Natural exit 1 in 0.372 s; connection closed; same HTTP diagnostic |
| Complete ready response | exit 0 in 0.285 s | exit 0 in 0.371 s |
| Complete 403 response | exit 1 in 0.318 s | exit 1 in 0.320 s |

The timeout cases print:

```text
::error::GitHub installation quota check exceeded the candidate-acquisition wait budget.
```

Both 403 controls retain:

```text
::error::Could not inspect GitHub installation quota (HTTP 403; request ID LOCAL-PROOF).
```

The focused suite covers both stalled response stages, timer cleanup after success/error, and the existing reset-wait behavior. The final test changes add 57 net lines, recorded in their own `config/test-lines-allocations/quota-response-deadline.txt` allocation. Narrow strict TypeScript, syntax, formatting, and scoped lint including type-aware checks were checked; no full local test suite was run.

Limits: this proves the shipped script's timeout and connection lifecycle through real local HTTP, not a GitHub outage or an actual release dispatch. Local Vitest used an isolated minimal source closure with one worker; the repository's standard broader lanes remain PR CI's responsibility. No workflow, permissions, credentials, dependency, or shared test-budget scalar changes.

Final head: `cb2cc32186e9ab84f4179b06231ed18204e0f222`. Exact-head focused suite: 7/7 passed. Native staged test-line gate: 6,597,886 lines against ceiling 6,597,891. The exact-head repeat of all five real HTTP cases also passes; stalled headers/body exit naturally in 1.119/1.086 s, and stalled 403 exits in 0.366 s, all with connection closure before fixture cleanup.

CI follow-up: the initial `check-lint` failure was caused by the new test rejecting with `AbortSignal.reason`, whose type is unconstrained. The test now preserves Error reasons and wraps other values in Error, with no casts or rule suppression. The same type-aware rule fails on the old test and passes on the fix locally (Oxlint 1.88, 266 rules); hosted CI uses 1.89 and is the final full-lane check. Production code is unchanged by this follow-up. The final-head [hosted CI run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/42629323570) now passes, including `check-lint`; the `openclaw/ci-gate` and dependency review also pass.

<details>
<summary>Standalone real-HTTP reproduction harness</summary>

Save this as `/tmp/quota-proof.mjs`, then run `node /tmp/quota-proof.mjs "$PWD/scripts/wait-for-github-api-quota.mjs"` from either checkout. The 2.5-second harness cleanup bounds the broken baseline; `forced: false` and connection closure must come from the CLI on the fix. Only the local fixture receives the synthetic token.

```js
import http from 'node:http';
import {spawn} from 'node:child_process';
const records=[];
const script=process.argv[2];
for(const mode of ['headers-stall','body-stall','ready','forbidden','forbidden-stall']) {
 const sockets=new Set(); let requested=false, closed=false, cleaning=false;
 const server=http.createServer((req,res)=>{
  requested=req.url==='/rate_limit' && req.headers.authorization==='Bearer fixture-token';
  if(mode==='headers-stall') return;
  res.writeHead(mode.startsWith('forbidden')?403:200,{'content-type':'application/json','x-github-request-id':'LOCAL-PROOF','connection':'close'});
  if(mode==='body-stall'||mode==='forbidden-stall') {res.write('{"resources":');return;}
  res.end(JSON.stringify({resources:{core:{remaining:10,limit:5000,reset:Math.floor(Date.now()/1000)+60}}}));
 });
 server.on('connection',socket=>{sockets.add(socket);socket.on('close',()=>{sockets.delete(socket);if(!cleaning)closed=true;});});
 await new Promise(resolve=>server.listen(0,'127.0.0.1',resolve));
 const began=performance.now();
 const child=spawn(process.execPath,[script,'--max-wait-seconds','1'],{env:{...process.env,GH_TOKEN:'fixture-token',GITHUB_API_URL:`http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}`},stdio:['ignore','pipe','pipe']});
 let stdout='',stderr='',forced=false,closedBeforeForcedKill=null;
 child.stdout.on('data',d=>stdout+=d);child.stderr.on('data',d=>stderr+=d);
 const timeout=setTimeout(()=>{closedBeforeForcedKill=closed;forced=true;child.kill('SIGKILL');},2500);
 const [code,signal]=await new Promise(resolve=>child.on('close',(code,signal)=>resolve([code,signal])));
 clearTimeout(timeout);
 const seconds=(performance.now()-began)/1000;
 const pass=requested&&!forced&&(mode==='ready'?code===0&&stderr.includes('quota ready'):code===1)&&(!mode.endsWith('stall')||closed);
 records.push({mode,requested,code,signal,seconds:Number(seconds.toFixed(3)),forced,closedBeforeForcedKill,connectionClosedBeforeCleanup:closed,stdout,stderr,pass});
 cleaning=true;server.closeAllConnections();await new Promise(resolve=>server.close(resolve));
}
console.log(JSON.stringify(records,null,2));
process.exitCode=records.every(r=>r.pass)?0:1;
```

</details>

Independent review of the complete final diff passed with no unresolved findings.

